      "question_number": 2,
      "question_max_mark": 28,
      "part_label": "c",
      "marks": 2,
      "markscheme_text": "METHOD 1\nuses $\\sin\\theta=\\frac{opp}{hyp}$\n$$\\frac{y/2}{x}=\\sin\\left(\\frac{\\pi}{n}\\right)$$\n$$y=2x\\sin\\left(\\frac{\\pi}{n}\\right)$$\n\nMETHOD 2\nuses Pythagoras' theorem $\\left(\\frac{y}{2}\\right)^{2}+h^{2}=x^{2}$ and $h=x\\cos\\left(\\frac{\\pi}{n}\\right)$\n$$\\left(\\frac{y}{2}\\right)^{2}+\\left(x\\cos\\left(\\frac{\\pi}{n}\\right)\\right)^{2}=x^{2} \\left(y^{2}=4x^{2}(1-\\cos^{2}\\left(\\frac{\\pi}{n}\\right))\\right)$$\n$$=4x^{2}\\sin^{2}\\left(\\frac{\\pi}{n}\\right)$$\n$$y=2x\\sin\\left(\\frac{\\pi}{n}\\right)$$\n\nMETHOD 3\nuses the cosine rule\n$$y^{2}=2x^{2}-2x^{2}\\cos\\left(\\frac{2\\pi}{n}\\right) \\left(=2x^{2}\\left(1-\\cos\\left(\\frac{2\\pi}{n}\\right)\\right)\\right)$$\n$$=4x^{2}\\sin^{2}\\left(\\frac{\\pi}{n}\\right)$$\n$$y=2x\\sin\\left(\\frac{\\pi}{n}\\right)$$\n\nMETHOD 4\nuses the sine rule\n$$\\frac{y}{\\sin\\left(\\frac{2\\pi}{n}\\right)}=\\frac{x}{\\sin\\left(\\frac{\\pi}{2}-\\frac{\\pi}{n}\\right)}$$\n$$y\\cos\\left(\\frac{\\pi}{n}\\right)=2x\\sin\\left(\\frac{\\pi}{n}\\right)\\cos\\left(\\frac{\\pi}{n}\\right)$$\n$$y=2x\\sin\\left(\\frac{\\pi}{n}\\right)$$"
    },
