      "marks": 5,
      "markscheme_text": "METHOD 1 (geometric, finding r)\n$u_{4} = u_{1} r^{3}$ OR $125 = 27(r)^{3}$\n$r = \\frac{5}{3}$ (seen anywhere)\n$p = 27r$ OR $\\frac{125}{q} = \\frac{5}{3}$\n$p = 45$, $q = 75$\n\nMETHOD 2 (arithmetic)\n$u_{4} = u_{1}+3d$ OR $\\log_{8} 125 = \\log_{8} 27+3d$\n$d = \\log_{8}\\left(\\frac{5}{3}\\right)$ (seen anywhere)\n$\\log_{8} p = \\log_{8} 27 + \\log_{8}\\left(\\frac{5}{3}\\right)$ OR $\\log_{8} q = \\log_{8} 27 + 2\\log_{8}\\left(\\frac{5}{3}\\right)$\n$p = 45$, $q = 75$\n\nMETHOD 3 (geometric using proportion)\nrecognizing proportion\n$pq = 125\\times27$ OR $q^{2} = 125p$ OR $p^{2} = 27q$\ntwo correct proportion equations\nattempt to eliminate either p or q\n$q^{2} = 125\\times\\frac{125\\times27}{q}$ OR $p^{2} = 27\\times\\frac{125\\times27}{p}$\n$p = 45$, $q = 75$"
